{"content_id":"CL-LTG-C2-001-AUTHORITY","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-RIG","D-ELC"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Production Flow","lesson_identifier":"Course Boundary","block_identifier":"authority-state","question_identifier":"l2q2","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Course 2 builds lighting-system vocabulary, workflow and reasoning; it does not itself authorize rigging, energized electrical work, lift operation, fall-protection work, or employer-controlled technical changes.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Authority-state boundary; external qualifications and employer assignment remain separate."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-C2-002-DOCUMENTATION","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Documentation","lesson_identifier":"Labels and Patch","block_identifier":"traceability","question_identifier":"l2q3/l2q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Lighting documentation and labeling support traceability between equipment, cable paths, addressing/universe information and the current system state; exact document names and required fields vary by production.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Two-end labeling and patch documentation are treated as recurring professional practice, not a universal paperwork mandate."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-C2-003-CHANGE-CONTROL","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Documentation","lesson_identifier":"Revisions","block_identifier":"change-control","question_identifier":"l2q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A material lighting-system revision should move through the responsible lead/change process and the affected documentation should be brought back into agreement with the approved system state rather than changed silently.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact approval path varies by production, employer and client relationship."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-C2-004-OVERHEAD-RETENTION","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-RIG"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Installation","lesson_identifier":"Inspection and Handoff","block_identifier":"secondary-retention","question_identifier":"l2q6","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"If required overhead retention or another rigging-related condition appears missing or unresolved, the learner reports it through the responsible lead/site process and does not independently install, substitute, approve or alter rigging hardware from Course 2 knowledge alone.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"critical","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Recognition/report boundary only; no retention or rigging procedure is taught."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-C2-005-LAYERED-DIAGNOSIS","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Testing","lesson_identifier":"Troubleshooting","block_identifier":"layered-diagnosis","question_identifier":"l2q7/l2q11","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A lighting symptom can originate in different system layers, so useful troubleshooting reasoning isolates the affected layer and communicates before changing shared configuration rather than changing multiple variables at once.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Systems reasoning only; exact diagnostic actions remain product/system/role controlled."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-C2-006-MODE-MAPPING","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Control","lesson_identifier":"Fixture Mode and Console Mapping","block_identifier":"personality-mode-match","question_identifier":"l2q9","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The control-system definition/personality and the fixture's configured control mode must describe compatible parameter/channel behavior; a mismatch can produce missing or incorrect control responses without proving the fixture itself is defective.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"High-level mapping concept; no console-specific configuration procedure is implied."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-C2-007-LOADOUT-RISK","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-SHF"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Load-Out","lesson_identifier":"Strike and Handoff","block_identifier":"risk-context","question_identifier":"l2q12","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Load-out can combine fatigue, reduced visibility, schedule pressure and simultaneous multi-department movement, so the end of the show does not remove the need for deliberate communication, release and hazard awareness.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Hazard-recognition framing only; site/employer controls remain primary."}
{"content_id":"Q-LTG-C2-L2Q1","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Production Flow","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"l2q1","question_identifier":"l2q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"What is the best description of lighting production flow?","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored question."}
{"content_id":"QR-Q-LTG-C2-L2Q1","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Production Flow","lesson_identifier":"Knowledge Check","block_identifier":"l2q1-rationale","question_identifier":"l2q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Lighting production is a lifecycle from creative intent and technical planning through documentation, installation, testing, programming/operation and load-out; exact phase ownership varies by production.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW-0001."}
